---
import { sitePath } from '../data/site';
import AtlasLayout from '../layouts/AtlasLayout.astro';
import { atlas, isPublication } from '../data/atlas';
---
<AtlasLayout title="Sources"><section class="page-width content-page"><p class="eyebrow">Evidence provenance</p><h1>Trace every claim.</h1><p class="hero-description">Sources retain their study identity, inspected location and access limits. Multiple findings from the same report do not establish independent replication.</p>
<aside class="preview-notice"><span class="notice-symbol" aria-hidden="true">i</span><div><strong>{isPublication ? 'Reviewed claims retain source-access limitations' : 'Source access and coverage'}</strong>These bounded maps do not claim exhaustive literature coverage. Abstract or excerpt access is distinguished from a complete report.</div></aside>
{atlas.map(({profile, bundle}) => <section><h2>{profile.label}</h2><p><a href={sitePath(`/diseases/${profile.id}/#mechanism-outline`)}>Inspect the map's complete evidence outline</a></p><ul class="source-list">{bundle.sources.map(source => <li id={`${profile.id}-${source.id}`}><span class="record-label">{source.kind.replaceAll('_',' ')}</span><h3><a href={source.url}>{source.title}</a></h3><p>{source.citation}</p><p>Study identity: {source.studyId}. Inspected: {source.accessScope}.</p>{!!source.flags?.length && <p>Source flags: {source.flags.join(', ')}. Inspect the affected claims.</p>}<p>Linked evidence items: {bundle.evidenceItems.filter(evidence => evidence.sourceId === source.id).length} · Checks: {[...new Set(bundle.evidenceItems.filter(evidence => evidence.sourceId === source.id).map(evidence => evidence.retrievedAt))].join(', ')}.</p><ul>{bundle.claims.filter(claim => claim.evidenceItemIds.some(id => bundle.evidenceItems.find(item => item.id === id)?.sourceId === source.id)).map(claim => <li><a href={sitePath(`/diseases/${profile.id}/#claim-${claim.id}`)}>{claim.text}</a></li>)}</ul></li>)}</ul></section>)}
<h2>Source selection and corrections</h2><p>Primary studies, regulatory labels and sponsor status reports have distinct evidentiary roles. Treatment approval is scoped to its recorded jurisdiction and indication. A status announcement cannot establish efficacy.</p><p>Literature scans refresh known publications and record correction, retraction and concern flags. Flagged records require explicit reconciliation of affected claims. A successful scan produces a review queue and does not update a scientific release.</p><p><a href={sitePath('/methodology/#publication-policy')}>Read the scientific publication policy</a></p></section></AtlasLayout>
